decodeAt is operation
decodeAt purpose "Read the character UTF-8 encodes at a position as Python's strict decoder reads it: store its code point (or -1 when the bytes there are not UTF-8) and give how many bytes it took (for bytes that are not UTF-8, the longest start of a valid sequence, at least 1)"
decodeAt invariant decodesStrictly "\"Valid sequences give their code point and length; overlong forms, surrogates, code points past U+10FFFF, and cut sequences give -1 and the bytes of the valid start\""
decodeAt typeParameter none
decodeAt input text machine.Address copied
decodeAt input bytes Int64 copied
decodeAt input at Int64 copied
decodeAt input out machine.Address copied
decodeAt output Int64
decodeAt outputOwnedBy none
decodeAt raises none
decodeAt effect use machine.memory
decodeAt uses memoryAccess
decodeAt memoryHeap false
decodeAt async false
decodeAt maxRecursion none
decodeAt label begin loopKind none
decodeAt label begin within none
